WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.480
Where did he go?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.780
<i>This is bad, Aki-kun!</i>

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:38.440
<i>This choice is extremely meaningful for Kasumigaoka-senpai!</i>

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.440
<i>Do you understand that?</i>

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.820
Why can't you understand, you Morals!

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.150
That's not what I want to ask!

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.320
That's not what I'm asking!

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:56.240
Why do you always go after the wrong thing like that?!

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.420
Welcome home, Master!

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.550
Broadly speaking, there's two problems.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.620
First of all, as you get closer to the climax,

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.890
your text becomes too much like a novel.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.770
You describe the characters' expressions and psychology too much and in excessive detail.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:45.770
That makes the pacing of the game worse.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.370
The game has pictures and production too.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:52.290
There's no need to describe in the text what can be seen on the screen.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.420
If anything, it only gets in the way.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.950
Are you saying it would be better without my prose?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.460
In a visual novel, the player advances by pushing a button.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.120
But if it goes nowhere no matter how much you push,

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.310
it doesn't feel like you're making the story go forward.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.380
That is fatal for a game.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.980
And then the second problem.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.210
This is the most importan-

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.260
Enough!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.060
Are you trying to deny me while avoiding answering my question?

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.290
That's some nerve you've got there for a Morals-kun.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.820
I'm not denying you,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.090
nor your earlier work!

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:26.180
I'm only talking about this scenario for this game!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.590
Kasumigaoka-san...

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:29.170
I'm only talking about this scenario for this game!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.250
Listen now!

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:30.730
I'm saying something like that is not my problem!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.170
Um, could you please keep it down-

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.740
What do you mean, "something like that"?

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.840
It's our game!

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.220
The product of our souls which we're all working so hard on!

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.790
This scenario won't do!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.930
It's an amazing story, but for reasons which have nothing to do with that,

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.790
it doesn't work at all!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.530
It's so frustrating.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.050
I want to smack my earlier incompetent self for not realising it.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.330
Because this...

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.050
...is not the game I wanted to make.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.730
U-Utaha-senpa-

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.130
I-I'm sorry!

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.520
Uh, um...

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:15.980
Utaha-senpai!

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.640
It's not your fault, Utaha-senpai.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.040
It's my fault as the director.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.040
I didn't realise it since I just kept reading the text file.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.640
I got caught in the perfection and high level of the story.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.120
The second half in particular is clearly like a novel,

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.570
not the scenario for a game.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:41.990
But it's all right.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.160
We still have time.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.060
So let's fix the scenario.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:51.570
If you can't agree to it, no matter what, I can fix it.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:56.700
It'll probably fall in quality as a pure story,

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.070
but even so, I'll do it.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.540
I'm the director, after all.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.460
Even if you say you're not doing it, no matter what,

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:05.200
I will do it.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.230
<i>I see, so the scenario will be redone.</i>

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.490
Yeah.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.190
Aki-kun is fixing it himself.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.740
<i>What about Kasumigaoka Utaha?</i>

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:41.180
Apparently in his room with him.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.320
<i>I see.</i>

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.080
Huh?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.300
What happened to your usual "K-Kasumigaoka Utaha"?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.790
<i>Who do you think I am, Megumi?</i>

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.120
They're revising the scenario.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.130
Her scenario was just rejected.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.230
What could happen?

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.130
<i>I wonder if that's true.</i>

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:01.850
Well, if she's a creator.

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:05.940
I can more or less understand
how Kasumigaoka Utaha feels.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.050
<i>I see.</i>

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.390
And anyway,

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:11.270
I can't focus on people now.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.280
The fallout will hit me in due time,

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.410
so I'll have to make as much progress as I can now.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.950
<i>So you're not participating in the school festival?</i>

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.890
<i>Won't you appear in Miss Toyogasaki this year?</i>

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.380
<i>You won last year, didn't you?</i>

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:28.900
Well, that was a good excuse not to enter.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.170
<i>So I shouldn't disturb you too much either.</i>

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.100
<i>I'm hanging up, okay?</i>

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.500
Thanks for calling.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.460
Later.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.140
Crap, what'd I do...

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.050
Are you awake?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:27.800
I'm not sleeping!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.510
I'm not sleeping at all!

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.100
Good timing.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.480
I'm almost done with my check, too.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.480
Utaha-senpai...

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:46.150
Good morning, Morals-kun.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.080
Based on my own interpretation of your opinions,

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.100
I checked the contents of your revisions.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.020
Furthermore,

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:57.260
I've made comments on parts which I can't agree to and passages where you've clearly made a mistake,

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.140
as well as errors like typos and missing words,

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:01.990
as much as I could,

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:04.520
so let's discuss based on this.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:05.510
This much?

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:10.580
The manuscript for my Newcomer of the Year novel had about twice this many notes.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.920
By Machida-san.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:14.890
H-Hey, Utaha-senp-

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:18.080
It took me two years to get the number down to double digits.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.160
Honestly,

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.270
writing is a tough trade.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.570
Um, is this...

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.600
With that in mind...

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:30.970
Things wouldn't be so convenient that my first game scenario would pass on the first shot either, would they?

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.790
All right, Morals-kun,

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:37.790
let's start.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:38.990
Yes!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.660
I redid this with my changes to the text.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:44.840
What do you think?

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.940
Is it really fine to have nothing but dialogue like this?

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.680
I can't help but think it feels bland.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:55.200
A game has lots of other ingredients making it interesting.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.560
It's just fine for the basis to be bland.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.440
If we're talking about revisions like this,

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.440
once you get the hang of it, it's not that difficult, is it?

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:07.310
I'd get something like that done in one day.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.370
You don't need to go that far.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.040
It's enough to check the changes I make.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.290
Revising this is no major undertaking.

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:16.220
This is what's impossible.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.040
The two scenarios go in completely different directions.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.990
Certainly, the Meguri route is an adventure action plot,

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:25.050
and the Ruri route is about star-crossed love.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.550
In the Meguri route, he returns to the present day,

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.640
but in the Ruri route he ends up eternally wandering in between space-time.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.940
In the Meguri route everybody but Ruri becomes happy,

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:39.190
but in the Ruri route, she and the main character hold on to small happiness alone.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.040
So if you were to add these to one game, the theme would get blurred-

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.610
Why is that a bad thing?

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:49.790
Utaha-senpai, you're thinking like a novelist again!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:54.330
Having a hodgepodge of themes,
not knowing where it ends up going,

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:56.200
is the appeal of gal games!

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.580
There's two rules for gal games.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.790
Namely, the heroines must be cute,

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:02.710
and you must not be bound by rules!

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:04.510
S-So,

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:11.100
are you aiming for a haphazard game with two completely different routes?

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.970
No, not at all, Utaha-senpai.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.310
There will be three routes.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.690
Are you an idiot?

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.060
Maybe.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.480
Adding yet another route at this point?

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.320
And doing it this weekend?

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:32.390
Because Eriri has to have the complete scenario by Monday or she won't have enough time to do the event pictures.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.390
If that's the case,

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:36.040
why are you bringing up something this unreasonable now?

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:36.700
Because...

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:42.150
I can't help it with how charming all the heroines you've created are.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:49.590
I thought that I'd like to see a story
where all these heroines live happily.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:54.000
That may not be Kasumi Utako's literary style,

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.730
but with this many characters I love,

00:10:56.730 --> 00:11:00.600
it would be too painful for me to not have a future where they all become happy.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:04.740
You're right,

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.110
it's not my literary style.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.770
So that's why I won't write it.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:10.530
If that's the case-

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:12.070
Suffice it to say,

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.500
if you want to make it that much,

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.560
you can write it yourself.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.580
Although that's something a creator can't say to the director,

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:23.930
it's okay for a creator to say to a creator, right?

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:24.620
It's okay?

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.250
You came up with that silliness,

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.400
so you carry it to completion too.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.820
Is that okay?

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:36.600
Is it really okay to mix my clumsy scenario in with your scenario?

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.140
What are you saying?

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.870
It's been mixed in for a long time, hasn't it?

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:44.060
Your thing is inside me already, isn't it?

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.020
My revisions are in your scenario, that is!

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:49.160
Also, Morals-kun.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.940
Did you already forget what you said earlier?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:55.880
It's the rule to not be bound by rules.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.550
H-How about something like this?

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:04.680
You wrote all this in half a day?

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.590
Your speed honestly surprises me.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.830
I-Is that so?

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:12.350
Well, so far you did nothing but mass produce garbage.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:16.180
For example, this part.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.470
What was your intention when including this discussion?

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:25.690
Did you think this useless content can portray what the character is like?

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.920
Personality, feelings, relationships...

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:33.850
When you write, think about how you can continuously include information about those in the text.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:39.450
Pointless, verbose verbiage is a sign of
incompetence in games and novels alike.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.790
Since you apparently are confident enough to find fault with my writing,

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:44.410
I had you take care of this,

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.660
but this is merely a beginner's dabbling.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.240
So I have to rewrite it?

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:50.260
No.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:52.500
Write the rest first.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.850
The time for revisions is when you've finished writing.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.440
If you keep going back when you're not done yet,

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.620
you will never finish.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:02.510
But what if nothing I've written can be used?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.040
If that's the case,

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.140
I'll patch it up.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.850
Utaha-senpai...

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.400
Leave it to me!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:14.400
I'll help with your dabbling all I can!

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:18.610
Please don't say it in a way which makes it difficult to reply "please do".

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.400
No, Ruri.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.830
I will never abandon you!

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.860
We're going back together!

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:31.170
Meguri and Ruri and everybody has to be there!

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:33.990
I don't want it any other way!

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.220
How far in are you?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.410
At around the scene where he and Ruri separate.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.590
Let me see.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:16.670
Around here, we'll make a choice to run after Ruri, and branch the story.

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:20.170
How about something like this?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.520
Tell me if there are any problems.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.180
There is one.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:27.180
I'm so tired I can't tell.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.430
Sleep for a while.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.350
I'll keep at this for a little longer.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.350
Well then, wake me up in two hours.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.330
Got it.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.360
Good night.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.860
Can I turn off the lights?

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.570
Sure, go ahead.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:46.610
Good night.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.740
Here goes!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.160
Hiroyuki, you idiot!

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:32.370
Hey, Morals-kun.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:34.620
What?

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:39.340
Do you really think such a happy ending with no sorrow whatsoever could happen?

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.420
Wouldn't it be nice if it did?

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:42.420
Sorry to say,

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.830
but I think Ruri has no right to become happy.

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:47.580
The one who created her is saying that?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:50.460
I mean, she's an absolute yandere.

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:56.060
She even tries to eliminate Meguri and the other heroines to get the main character for herself.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:58.690
But I love her because of that.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:01.890
So which do you like more, her or Meguri?

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:04.630
I love both of them, of course!

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:08.400
They're the double main heroine we created, after all.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:12.450
I didn't mean it like that.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.800
Meguri and Ruri competing over the main character,

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.860
being jealous in a cute way,

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:20.030
everybody fed up with them, laughing...

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:23.690
Don't you want to see such a carefree ending?

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:30.100
Half of me thinks it's impossible, and
half of me wants to see what it'd be like.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:34.350
That's what the relationship between Ruri and Meguri is all about.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.330
I can't move.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.720
So regrettable.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:52.850
I could do whatever I wanted to you right now.

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:56.700
You're talking about beating me up, aren't you?

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:02.170
Sorry, Utaha-senpai.

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:04.260
You don't need to apologise.

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:08.330
But I broke your scenario.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.310
I changed the characters' personalities and the setting.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:16.350
Even though the changed characters live in a changed world,

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:19.750
those girls didn't die.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.330
They lived.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:26.010
They cried, laughed, and loved.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:30.390
Reading- I mean, playing it made me happy.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:31.810
It was fun.

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.360
Exciting.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.500
Utaha-senpai...

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:42.400
This is something nobody else, nor you alone or me alone, could make.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:46.960
Our completely original scenario.

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:18.910
And so we somehow finished the scenario.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:21.950
With this, I'm done with my part for good.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:26.400
I'd still like your help with various production issues.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:27.800
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:31.550
I'll have to start working on my light novel again soon.

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:35.270
By the way, may I ask one thing?

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:36.060
What is it?

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:44.520
Ruri is Sayuka from Metronome of Love, right?

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:48.230
I read both of them many times.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.700
It looks like it, doesn't it, Katou-san?

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.530
They both have a common model.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:19:02.040
An inexperienced, unsociable author had to take data from the closest possible place.

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:06.960
The gloomy, vengeful, unpleasant woman.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:11.800
She'd always been such a lonely character.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:21.060
So I wanted Main Character-kun to choose, if just this once.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.580
No, it's still not too late.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:43.540
I'm sure you can change that gloomy heroine to be more charming.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:47.080
What... should I do?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:54.930
No way,

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:57.930
I ended up surrounded by the other team.

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:01.680
Onii-chan!

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:05.710
Onii-chan.

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:10.440
Sheesh, Onii-chan.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.830
You're quite mean,

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.140
ignoring Ruri.

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.620
Ruri...

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.330
I was always calling to you.

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:30.020
For years,

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.480
for decades,

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.590
always, all the time.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.510
Katou...

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:39.350
Don't say "Katou" now,

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:41.850
Aki-kun.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:47.810
Because now I'm Ruri, Sayuka,

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:51.070
and...
